            <ArticleTitle>Reply to: Comment On: The cancer Warburg effect may be a testable example of the minimum entropy production rate principle.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1088/1478-3975/aa8ead</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We point that the minimum rate theorem [3] refers to internal entropy production (ΔSi), here calculated for the chemical reaction in the open cell system. We also point that In the steady-state open system the constant supply of glucose makes equivalent the minimum rate of entropy production per unit of time to the minimum rate of production of entropy per mole of glucose.</AbstractText>
